# Files that may hold a Key Vault secret data-plane command (check-manual-keyvault.py).
# Policy `secrets-write-only-entry` — Doc/Architecture/SecretsWriteOnlyEntry.
#
# Each line: <file or glob>  — <why it may hold one>. Only CODE the governed path executes is listed,
# never a doc or runbook (a documented break-glass step carries `kv-break-glass: <reason>` instead).
# The list only SHRINKS: an entry that no longer matches a file holding a command reds the gate.
# 🚨 "TRANSITIONAL" marks a governed verb that still READS a value (or checks existence with a value
# read). Migration step 3 in the design page rewrites each so the writer identity never needs `get`;
# the line goes when that rewrite lands.

# The writer's own verbs: set with tags, status from metadata, lifecycle. None reads a value.
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-kv-set  — writer verb: writes through --file, confirms by list-versions. TRANSITIONAL (policy secret-actions-interim-actions-lane): its --generate mode also runs as hosting-operator on the aks-ops lane until the writer identity is provisioned and every secret action runs in the in-cluster Job under it
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-kv-state  — writer verb: set-attributes / delete / recover / purge, no value
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-kv-purge  — teardown verb: deletes an instance's objects by prefix, no value read

# Governed provisioning verbs that still run as hosting-operator.
deploy/aks/operator/bin/_common.sh  — TRANSITIONAL: hosting::pg_password reads the server admin password to compose connection strings
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-kv-ensure  — TRANSITIONAL: the admin-password read for the connection string (existence is checked with `list`)
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-kv-copy  — TRANSITIONAL: copyFrom reads the source value to write the per-prefix copy
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-kv-rotate  — TRANSITIONAL: reads the vaulted registry key to compare before rotating
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-registry-register  — TRANSITIONAL: reads the held instance key and the bootstrap key to call the registry
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-signin-app  — writes the minted Entra client secret through --file; existence is checked with `list`, no value read
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-image-mirror  — TRANSITIONAL: reads the registry publisher password to push the mirror
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-pull-secret  — TRANSITIONAL: reads the registry pull key to render the image pull Secret
deploy/aks/operator/bin/hosting-deploy  — TRANSITIONAL: downloads the helm values half (helm-values-<release>); retired with the vault half

# Their behaviour suite and its stand-in binaries (they answer the commands, they do not run them).
deploy/aks/operator/test/run-tests.sh  — asserts the verbs write through --file, never print a value and never read one back
deploy/aks/operator/test/stubs/*/az  — stand-in az binaries for that suite

# This gate, which has to spell the commands it refuses.
.github/scripts/check-manual-keyvault.py  — the gate itself
